@group
    @title=Authoring Templates
    @brief=The section describes how to create your own template
    @ingroup=templates
    @key=authoringTemplates

    To save the documentation in a particular format a **template** is used. 

    There are a set of predefined templates, however you can create 
    your own templates. 

    When documentation is compiled from the source code, the compiler 
    builds up an XML document that contains all the documentation
    information. The schema of this document reflects the structure of
    the documentation. Check [link=modelXML]XML model[/link] for more details. 

    The template is a set of one or more XSLT transformations that 
    creates one or more text documents (e.g. other HTML for web documentation or 
    Microsoft HTMLHelp sources, or XML for XMLDoc). In order to facilitate 
    the procedure approach to the development (as XSLT functional approach is 
    not always easy to learn for developers) and to extend XSLT 1.0 with 
    ability to create multiple output files, a set of 
    [link=xpathFunctions]XPATH extension functions[/link] is
     provided for these templates.

    As a result, the documentation generator has all features of a 
    code generator and it also can be used, for example, to create a 
    documentation source on the base of assembly structure or 
    doxygen output. 

    If you look for examples, please check `template` folder 
    of the docgen git repository. All the standard templates
    are located there. 
@end
